        "de-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "69040ee2-4e4f-389e-985d-b7fde1591e2a",
                "word": "wiewohl",
                "pos": "conj",
                "lang_code": "de",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6f80d0ae-9eb9-375a-81a1-494a748a4666",
                        "entry_id": "69040ee2-4e4f-389e-985d-b7fde1591e2a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "obwohl, obzwar, wenngleich; wenn auch, obschon"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "literary"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a03903dc-1057-4ff9-abe6-1871738919b6",
                                "sense_id": "6f80d0ae-9eb9-375a-81a1-494a748a4666",
                                "text": "„Wiewohl die Handlungen bei dieser ersten Zusammenkunft vielleicht von weniger Gewicht sind als in der zweiten, so kann man sich doch nicht eines Gefühls von Entsetzen und sehr peinlicher Gedanken erwehren, wenn man hört, daß die kleine Hortense dabei zu dem Frevler gesagt haben will: ‚Du beleidigst ja den lieben Gott.‘“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "aab292a3-3d54-4ffc-bb52-82b3c48a483c",
                                "sense_id": "6f80d0ae-9eb9-375a-81a1-494a748a4666",
                                "text": "Unsere Arbeit wird recht einfach sein, wiewohl ich noch nicht alle Details kenne."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2399aac9-7739-47d1-8cdf-5afb8df467f4",
                                "sense_id": "6f80d0ae-9eb9-375a-81a1-494a748a4666",
                                "text": "„[…] und mein Vater, wiewohl dick und fett, besaß viel persönliche Grazie und legte stets Gewicht auf eine gewählte und durchsichtige Ausdrucksweise.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bdfc6812-f475-4066-a5b1-748f2b97327a",
                                "sense_id": "6f80d0ae-9eb9-375a-81a1-494a748a4666",
                                "text": "„Als hingebungsvoller Naturforscher hatte er ein noch weit größeres Problem, nämlich die riesigen Beweislücken, die zwischen seinen Ideen vom Ursprung der Sprache klafften, wiewohl sie es doch war, die das menschliche Verhalten so grundlegend von jedem tierischen unterschied.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ace1b708-2bd7-4506-adf8-8d1426bb1161",
                        "source_entry_id": "69040ee2-4e4f-389e-985d-b7fde1591e2a",
                        "source_sense_id": "6f80d0ae-9eb9-375a-81a1-494a748a4666",
                        "source_sense_description": "gehoben: obwohl, obzwar, wenngleich; (in verkürzten Konstruktionen:) wenn auch, obschon",
                        "target_lang_word": "although",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "although",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9e07aa28-a548-3757-a9d5-0e5a142ca1c5",
                                        "entry_id": "b3ddc799-961b-31e8-8efa-1cd2855466fc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Though, even though, in spite of or despite the fact that: introducing a clause that expresses a concession."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "986be2ce-2ef1-4ad5-a6cf-d473f444cd26",
                                                "sense_id": "9e07aa28-a548-3757-a9d5-0e5a142ca1c5",
                                                "text": "Although it was very muddy, the football game went on."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b23c010-4e31-48a5-978d-deb831777ede",
                                                "sense_id": "9e07aa28-a548-3757-a9d5-0e5a142ca1c5",
                                                "text": "The patients, (al)though getting stronger, will not come off their medications."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44dda5db-ed69-4498-84ec-5ba62ec1bbea",
                                                "sense_id": "9e07aa28-a548-3757-a9d5-0e5a142ca1c5",
                                                "text": "Although proven, the accusation was ignored by the court."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ff4b368-d712-4ddf-b78a-1224c77872da",
                                                "sense_id": "9e07aa28-a548-3757-a9d5-0e5a142ca1c5",
                                                "text": "And moreover, much leſs can this poyſonouíneſs be produced from the Lead. For although it being long detained in the Body, and there reſolved, likeunto other Metals, (if it contract any ruſtineſs) it may poſſibly do hurt: but yet neverthleſs, that in this its moment any paſſage through the Body there ſhould be any poyſon imprinted by it upon the Body, this can no waybe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f6aa4324-57b7-4410-a290-c9ec189a9345",
                                                "sense_id": "9e07aa28-a548-3757-a9d5-0e5a142ca1c5",
                                                "text": "Although the Celebrity was almost impervious to sarcasm, he was now beginning to exhibit visible signs of uneasiness, the consciousness dawning upon him that his eccentricity was not receiving the ovation it merited."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77c909ac-14ca-47c3-93e1-a41d35d6c427",
                                                "sense_id": "9e07aa28-a548-3757-a9d5-0e5a142ca1c5",
                                                "text": "The story struck the depressingly familiar note with which true stories ring in the tried ears of experienced policemen.[…]The second note, the high alarum, not so familiar and always important since it indicates the paramount sin in Man's private calendar, took most of them by surprise although they had been well prepared."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "03dee591-6a3d-433d-8907-9ab28d6061b8",
                                                "sense_id": "9e07aa28-a548-3757-a9d5-0e5a142ca1c5",
                                                "text": "With the north London derby to come at the weekend, Spurs boss Harry Redknapp opted to rest many of his key players, although he brought back Aaron Lennon after a month out through injury."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2f6ea81e-2bec-4e39-9897-724f59d5b50b",
                                                "sense_id": "9e07aa28-a548-3757-a9d5-0e5a142ca1c5",
                                                "text": "Although there are dozens of different types of gems, among the best known and most important are diamond, ruby and sapphire, emerald and other gem forms of the mineral beryl, chrysoberyl, tanzanite, tsavorite, topaz and jade."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9ccea8b0-bfbc-3dce-a0bd-8729c20c702e",
                                        "entry_id": "b3ddc799-961b-31e8-8efa-1cd2855466fc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "But, except."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87bdafaa-d673-4e27-a5da-35797e79fa8b",
                                                "sense_id": "9ccea8b0-bfbc-3dce-a0bd-8729c20c702e",
                                                "text": "It was difficult, although not as difficult as we had expected."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2f1fe41f-5582-4b59-a8ac-cd8c510fd5dd",
                        "source_entry_id": "69040ee2-4e4f-389e-985d-b7fde1591e2a",
                        "source_sense_id": "6f80d0ae-9eb9-375a-81a1-494a748a4666",
                        "source_sense_description": "gehoben: obwohl, obzwar, wenngleich; (in verkürzten Konstruktionen:) wenn auch, obschon",
                        "target_lang_word": "bien que",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bien que",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5b90a56d-52b2-37b6-8d38-480dbe48ba52",
                                        "entry_id": "3279f090-93d5-3b33-81cc-1e0b86f624a2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Conjonction de subordination introduisant une concession."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ed79f53e-550e-42eb-84aa-f49ea7f014ae",
                                                "sense_id": "5b90a56d-52b2-37b6-8d38-480dbe48ba52",
                                                "text": "La brume nous enveloppa de nouveau, bien que le soleil brillât dans une échappée de ciel au dessus de nos têtes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "371c3265-a1ed-447d-a0ba-8eed5eb83744",
                                                "sense_id": "5b90a56d-52b2-37b6-8d38-480dbe48ba52",
                                                "text": "Elle ne salait les mets qu’après la cuisson, bien qu’elle sût à quel point la fadeur lui en était désagréable."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f5d834e9-b19f-4d61-9f17-d6095a02d409",
                                                "sense_id": "5b90a56d-52b2-37b6-8d38-480dbe48ba52",
                                                "text": "L'été s’annonçait assez beau, bien qu’il crachinât de temps à autre sur la frange en bordure de mer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96162260-9b24-45b5-8b81-679f84970f5f",
                                                "sense_id": "5b90a56d-52b2-37b6-8d38-480dbe48ba52",
                                                "text": "Puis elles éclatent de rire, bien qu’elles soient dans leurs petits souliers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e18ba2d-13de-47fd-9d03-f495d17f5f9e",
                                                "sense_id": "5b90a56d-52b2-37b6-8d38-480dbe48ba52",
                                                "text": "Je suis allée à la danse ce matin, bien que je sois malade"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "24c691c5-98d8-415b-8ba6-4cf062dac9cc",
                        "source_entry_id": "69040ee2-4e4f-389e-985d-b7fde1591e2a",
                        "source_sense_id": "6f80d0ae-9eb9-375a-81a1-494a748a4666",
                        "source_sense_description": "gehoben: obwohl, obzwar, wenngleich; (in verkürzten Konstruktionen:) wenn auch, obschon",
                        "target_lang_word": "même si",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "même si",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8becba30-eb06-3977-93b2-5414006f4b2d",
                                        "entry_id": "1e81c934-38f8-3db0-a308-9959ac5b5721",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Conjonction indiquant qu'en dépit d'un élément vrai ou faux, une situation reste indifférente."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a2cefb8-10e9-4815-9349-e2be33b6cb02",
                                                "sense_id": "8becba30-eb06-3977-93b2-5414006f4b2d",
                                                "text": "Peut-être suis-je découragé par la menace d’une guerre. Mais il y aura toujours cette menace, même si la guerre n’éclate pas. Il faut faire als ob [comme si], comme dit Adler."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87324d18-6ee8-41b2-831e-e5b3079b00e0",
                                                "sense_id": "8becba30-eb06-3977-93b2-5414006f4b2d",
                                                "text": "Tourane est tombée. Mais au prix de lourdes pertes des deux côtés, même si je sais très bien que tout le monde se moque bien des morts annamites."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "02c405b5-cd62-4986-b87b-bbe19c7ac5a4",
                                                "sense_id": "8becba30-eb06-3977-93b2-5414006f4b2d",
                                                "text": "Même si les intentions du gouvernement Guy Mollet étaient libérales, le poids des contraintes a poussé ce gouvernement à pratiquer la guerre à outrance, au point d'hypothéquer tout le reste de son action, […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fddc6579-8140-4967-b07f-596b351d59d4",
                                                "sense_id": "8becba30-eb06-3977-93b2-5414006f4b2d",
                                                "text": "[…]; c'est en effet un roman dont le cadre est essentiellement rural, même si un certain nombre de scènes se déroulent au château, […]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
